{
  "id": "pacs.009.001.08",
  "short": "pacs.009",
  "name": "FinancialInstitutionCreditTransfer",
  "domain": "pacs",
  "label": "Financial Institution Credit Transfer",
  "direction": "bank → bank",
  "mtEquivalent": [
    "MT202",
    "MT202COV",
    "MT205",
    "MT205COV"
  ],
  "related": [
    "pacs.008",
    "pacs.002",
    "pacs.004"
  ],
  "summary": "Moves funds where both the debtor and the creditor are financial institutions — a bank paying another bank on its own behalf, rather than for a customer.",
  "whenUsed": "Three distinct jobs share this one message. Plain bank-to-bank transfers (the MT202 case: treasury settlement, nostro funding, liquidity moves). Cover payments (the MT202COV case: the funds leg that settles a separate customer pacs.008 travelling by a different route). And, with the ADV variant, advice of a transfer. Which job it is doing is signalled by whether Underlying Customer Credit Transfer is present.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Remittance Information does not exist in this message. If you need to tell a creditor what a payment is for, it is a customer transfer and belongs in pacs.008.",
    "A cover payment carries the underlying customer's details inside UndrlygCstmrCdtTrf purely so the receiving agent can sanctions-screen them. Those details are informational — the money movement is bank to bank, and crediting the underlying creditor from a pacs.009 COV is a serious processing error.",
    "Debtor and Creditor here are BranchAndFinancialInstitutionIdentification, not Party — so they have a BICFI, not a Name-and-address Party block. Code that reuses a pacs.008 party parser on this message will not find what it expects."
  ],
